Eulerian Path (Graph Theory)
===================================

* In Eulerian path theory, the "degree" of a vertex is the number of edges incident to that vertex, with a loop contributing two to the degree.
* An undirected graph has an Eulerian path if and only if;

        ->All vertices with a non-zero degree belong to a single connected component. 

        ex:- 3 - 0 - 2    1   ,contains an Eulerian path. 

        ->Exactly zero or two vertices have an odd degree (number of connected edges).


